<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_1d16c965-447a-a8a1-681e-430545c46cb7" id="_1d16c965-447a-a8a1-681e-430545c46cb7"></a>The base score as reported by the event source. See specific usage.</p>
</div>

<div><a name="_e7962a8a-e1e3-03e4-b6f4-d793fb38c8d6" id="_e7962a8a-e1e3-03e4-b6f4-d793fb38c8d6"></a><h3>9.9.37.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>BIOS Date</h3>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_e0cd49c2-23d4-d95b-e9e1-70eb418c5ab8" id="_e0cd49c2-23d4-d95b-e9e1-70eb418c5ab8"></a>The BIOS date. For example: 03/31/16.</p>
</div>

<div><a name="_3559dfbe-b64a-c46f-5a12-905be5be646a" id="_3559dfbe-b64a-c46f-5a12-905be5be646a"></a><h3>9.9.38.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>BIOS Manufacturer</h3>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_152d4e03-18a8-8bea-3f32-a7ac4b8015b7" id="_152d4e03-18a8-8bea-3f32-a7ac4b8015b7"></a>The BIOS manufacturer. For example: LENOVO.</p>
</div>

<div><a name="_06cc03fe-8bc6-02f1-abf6-62e5864f9c55" id="_06cc03fe-8bc6-02f1-abf6-62e5864f9c55"></a><h3>9.9.39.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>BIOS Version</h3>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_1a143ff7-25f6-1425-6922-7419ca8308c3" id="_1a143ff7-25f6-1425-6922-7419ca8308c3"></a>The BIOS version. For example: LENOVO G5ETA2WW (2.62).</p>
</div>

<div><a name="_6a892563-b810-3e2f-495b-c8ec28ee26dc" id="_6a892563-b810-3e2f-495b-c8ec28ee26dc"></a><h3>9.9.40.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Boundary</h3>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ec0da90d-d1e1-8a95-fb33-a564f90c7bf3" id="_ec0da90d-d1e1-8a95-fb33-a564f90c7bf3"></a>The boundary of the connection, normalized to the caption of 'boundary_id'. In the case of 'Other', it is defined by the event source.  For cloud connections, this translates to the traffic-boundary(same VPC, through IGW, etc.). For traditional networks, this is described as Local, Internal, or External.</p>
</div>

<div><a name="_193f80bf-9638-7bf1-a69d-73e315b3471f" id="_193f80bf-9638-7bf1-a69d-73e315b3471f"></a><h3>9.9.41.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Boundary ID</h3>

