</div>

<div><a name="_cf1a83bd-7131-cadc-e937-c7c772c87fc1" id="_cf1a83bd-7131-cadc-e937-c7c772c87fc1"></a><h3>9.9.354.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Package URL</h3>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_b00f5931-064c-fb55-1448-969d9b4645d4" id="_b00f5931-064c-fb55-1448-969d9b4645d4"></a>A purl is a URL string used to identify and locate a software package in a mostly universal and uniform way across programing languages, package managers, packaging conventions, tools, APIs and databases.</p>
</div>

<div><a name="_24d637ca-2840-786a-85d3-79bbda1eca66" id="_24d637ca-2840-786a-85d3-79bbda1eca66"></a><h3>9.9.355.<span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Proxy Connection Info</h3>

